WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:02.531
Easy Fables. Part 4.

00:00:02.531 --> 00:00:04.448
The Fox and the Stork.

00:00:04.448 --> 00:00:07.288
A fox asked a stork to come to dinner.

00:00:07.288 --> 00:00:09.861
He put some soup on a flat plate.

00:00:09.861 --> 00:00:12.151
The fox could drink it easily.

00:00:12.151 --> 00:00:17.537
But the stork had a long, thin mouth, and she could not get any soup at all.

00:00:17.537 --> 00:00:19.793
The fox laughed to himself.

00:00:19.793 --> 00:00:23.487
"I am sorry you do not like my soup," he said.

00:00:23.487 --> 00:00:26.199
"Do not be sorry," said the stork.

00:00:26.199 --> 00:00:28.834
"Please come to dinner at my house tomorrow."

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:31.576
The next day the fox went to her house.

00:00:31.576 --> 00:00:36.540
The stork put the food in a tall jar with a small opening at the top.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:39.772
She could reach the food easily with her long mouth.

00:00:39.772 --> 00:00:42.828
But the fox could not get his nose into the jar.

00:00:42.828 --> 00:00:44.404
He went home hungry.

00:00:44.404 --> 00:00:48.541
If you play tricks on others, they may do the same to you.

00:00:48.541 --> 00:00:50.848
The Old Lion and the Fox.

00:00:50.848 --> 00:00:54.092
A lion was too old to catch animals for food.

00:00:54.092 --> 00:00:55.768
So he made a plan.

00:00:55.768 --> 00:00:59.868
He lay down in his cave and told everyone that he was sick.

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:02.206
The animals felt sorry for him.

00:01:02.206 --> 00:01:05.015
One by one, they came to visit him.

00:01:05.015 --> 00:01:08.008
And one by one, the lion ate them.

00:01:08.008 --> 00:01:10.035
At last the fox came.

00:01:10.035 --> 00:01:12.369
But she did not go into the cave.

00:01:12.369 --> 00:01:15.736
She stood outside and asked, "How are you today?"

00:01:15.736 --> 00:01:18.441
"I am very sick," said the lion.

00:01:18.441 --> 00:01:20.512
"Come inside and talk to me."

00:01:20.512 --> 00:01:23.628
"No, thank you," said the fox.

00:01:23.628 --> 00:01:26.675
"I can see many footprints going into your cave.

00:01:26.675 --> 00:01:29.160
But I cannot see any coming out."

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:32.352
A wise person learns from what happens to others.

00:01:32.352 --> 00:01:34.026
The Bundle of Sticks.

00:01:34.026 --> 00:01:38.325
A father had three sons who were always fighting with each other.

00:01:38.325 --> 00:01:40.605
He wanted to teach them something.

00:01:40.605 --> 00:01:44.206
One day he brought them a bundle of sticks tied together.

00:01:44.206 --> 00:01:46.320
"Break this," he said.

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.804
Each son tried as hard as he could.

00:01:48.804 --> 00:01:51.063
But nobody could break the bundle.

00:01:51.063 --> 00:01:53.632
Then the father took the sticks apart.

00:01:53.632 --> 00:01:56.023
He gave one stick to each son.

00:01:56.023 --> 00:01:58.230
"Now break them," he said.

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:00.422
They broke the sticks easily.

00:02:00.422 --> 00:02:03.403
"You are like these sticks," said the father.

00:02:03.403 --> 00:02:06.551
"If you stay together, nobody can hurt you.

00:02:06.551 --> 00:02:11.780
But if each of you stands alone, you will be broken as easily as one stick."

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:13.457
Together we are strong.

00:02:13.457 --> 00:02:15.435
The Frog and the Ox.

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:18.512
A little frog saw a big ox in a field.

00:02:18.512 --> 00:02:20.768
He ran home to tell his father.

00:02:20.768 --> 00:02:23.699
"Father, I saw a terrible animal!

00:02:23.699 --> 00:02:25.728
It was as big as a mountain."

00:02:25.728 --> 00:02:29.433
"That was only the farmer's ox," said the old frog.

00:02:29.433 --> 00:02:31.136
"It is not so big.

00:02:31.136 --> 00:02:33.922
I can make myself just as big as that."

00:02:33.922 --> 00:02:37.043
And he took a deep breath and blew himself up.

00:02:37.043 --> 00:02:39.828
"Was he as big as this?" he asked.

00:02:39.828 --> 00:02:43.213
"Oh, much bigger," said the little frog.

00:02:43.213 --> 00:02:46.069
The old frog blew himself up some more.

00:02:46.069 --> 00:02:47.428
"As big as this?"

00:02:47.428 --> 00:02:49.857
"Bigger, father, bigger."

00:02:49.857 --> 00:02:55.809
So the old frog took one more deep breath, and blew, and blew, and blew.

00:02:55.809 --> 00:02:57.341
And then he burst.

00:02:57.341 --> 00:02:59.779
Do not try to be something you are not.

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.408
The Cat and the Bell.

00:03:01.408 --> 00:03:03.542
The mice had a big problem.

00:03:03.542 --> 00:03:07.576
There was a cat in the house, and she caught many of them.

00:03:07.576 --> 00:03:10.386
So they held a meeting to decide what to do.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.962
A young mouse stood up.

00:03:12.962 --> 00:03:15.420
"I have a good idea," he said.

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:18.102
"Let us put a bell around the cat's neck.

00:03:18.102 --> 00:03:22.164
Then we will always hear her coming, and we can run away."

00:03:22.164 --> 00:03:25.168
All the mice thought this was a wonderful idea.

00:03:25.168 --> 00:03:26.705
They were very happy.

00:03:26.705 --> 00:03:28.801
Then an old mouse stood up.

00:03:28.801 --> 00:03:31.215
"It is a good plan," he said.

00:03:31.215 --> 00:03:33.224
"But I have one question.

00:03:33.224 --> 00:03:35.631
Who is going to put the bell on the cat?"

00:03:35.631 --> 00:03:37.071
Nobody answered.

00:03:37.071 --> 00:03:39.181
It is easy to have an idea.

00:03:39.181 --> 00:03:40.826
It is hard to do it.
